android/maxima-core/ is the shared core of the Maxima transport, vendored from
https://github.com/eurobuddha/maxima at commit 6e001754428623b891bc582b05fe505c1f96f37c
(its core/src/main tree, unmodified: 88 files, checked byte for byte against
that commit on 2026-09-22). It is what makes this app a Maxima node rather than
an app asking another app to be one for it. Java 11, no runtime dependencies.

That repository declares no licence, so its author was asked, on 2026-09-21,
whether Mininotes may be published with this tree inside it and credited to
them. They answered on 2026-09-22, in a private message: "go for it" (typed
"fo for it"), "with my blessing", "open source is free although I do appreciate
you asking". So the tree is redistributed here with its author's permission and
credit, and nothing more is claimed for it: it is not under this project's
LICENSE, the GPL is not put on it, and anybody who wants
the Maxima transport for their own work should take it from its own repository
and its author rather than from here. The same credit is beside the code, in
android/maxima-core/NOTICE. See docs/MAXIMA-TRANSPORT.md.

SHA3-256 is not vendored: Android provides none at any version, and rather than
take a cryptography library for one function, org.mininotes.android.Sha3 is an
implementation of Keccak-f[1600] checked against the published NIST answers.

